/**
 * Arizona Real Estate Salesperson Prelicense (90 hours) — module question bank.
 *
 * ARIZONA IS 96 HOURS, NOT 90, AND THE COURSES ARE SEPARATE. A.R.S. § 32-2124(B) requires 90 hours of
 * prelicensure instruction. § 32-2124(L) then requires, "AFTER COMPLETING THE REQUIREMENTS OF SUBSECTION B,"
 * a further SIX HOURS OF INSTRUCTION IN REAL ESTATE CONTRACT LAW AND CONTRACT WRITING, certified to the
 * Department AT THE TIME OF APPLICATION. This bank covers the 90. The six are a separate course with its
 * own bank in config/arizona/contract-writing-6-question-bank.mjs.
 *
 * TWENTY-SEVEN OF THE NINETY MAY NOT BE WAIVED. § 32-2124(B)'s closing sentence lets the commissioner waive
 * the prelicensure course requirement for an out-of-state licensee "OTHER THAN THE TWENTY-SEVEN-HOUR
 * ARIZONA-SPECIFIC COURSE," and A.A.C. R4-28-401(A)(2) repeats it. MODULES 10, 11, 12 AND 13 ARE THAT
 * 27 HOURS — 7 + 7 + 7 + 6 — and each is flagged arizonaSpecific: true below. Modules 01 through 09 are the
 * remaining 63 hours of general content, at 7.0 hours each.
 *
 * ARIZONA IS A FIDUCIARY STATE AND SAYS SO IN THE FIRST SENTENCE OF ITS DUTY RULE. A.A.C. R4-28-1101(A):
 * "A licensee owes a FIDUCIARY DUTY to the client and shall protect and promote the client's interests. The
 * licensee shall also DEAL FAIRLY with all other parties to a transaction." This project has built courses
 * for states that legislated the opposite — Washington provides that its duties are statutory and NOT
 * fiduciary, and Oklahoma abrogated the common-law fiduciary duties by statute. NO ITEM IN THIS BANK MAY
 * PRESENT ARIZONA AS A STATUTORY-DUTY STATE, and several items exist to catch a student who arrived with
 * another state's account.
 *
 * THREE ARIZONA PROVISIONS THAT REVERSE WHAT A STUDENT MAY EXPECT:
 *   R4-28-1101(B)(1)-(2) — written disclosure to ALL OTHER PARTIES of information that EITHER the seller or
 *                          the buyer "is or may be unable to perform."
 *   R4-28-1101(I)        — an AFFIRMATIVE duty to OBTAIN information material to the client's interests.
 *                          Washington's statute expressly removes any duty to investigate; Arizona's rule
 *                          runs the other way.
 *   R4-28-802(B)         — the duty to submit all offers "IS NOT RELEASED ... BY THE CLIENT'S ACCEPTANCE OF
 *                          AN OFFER" unless the client instructs IN WRITING to cease, or the listing
 *                          agreement, lease or purchase contract provides otherwise.
 *
 * THE COURSE EXAMINATION IS NOT THIS BANK. A.A.C. R4-28-401(A)(1) sets a passing score of 75 PERCENT, and
 * A.R.S. § 32-2124(B) requires the examination be PROCTORED IN PERSON. R4-28-403 requires weekly
 * examinations and provides that qualifying to take or passing a licence examination is NOT a licence. The
 * items here gate progression, are visible by design, and the 80 percent engagement threshold and 100
 * percent applied threshold are STATECOURSE STANDARDS, not Department figures.
 *
 * Each module carries one applied item, five engagement items and five remediation items. The correct
 * answer is authored at index 0 and permuted deterministically per item id at delivery. The public delivery
 * path strips correctChoice and rationale, and a test proves it.
 *
 * WHAT WAS NOT OBTAINED, AND WHICH THEREFORE APPEARS IN NO ITEM: the Department's PRESCRIBED PRELICENSURE
 * COURSE CONTENT, which R4-28-401(D) says the Department will provide on request; any outline for the
 * 27-hour Arizona-specific course; A.R.S. §§ 32-2151, 32-2151.01 and 32-2174 and the trust account and
 * records-retention statutes; A.R.S. § 32-2153 and every disciplinary ground and penalty; Arizona's
 * residential seller disclosure statutes; the subdivided land, unsubdivided land and time-share statutes,
 * including when a public report is required; Arizona's statute of frauds; Arizona's landlord-tenant
 * statutes; A.R.S. § 32-2101(2)'s definition of advertising; any Department form, examination content
 * outline or candidate handbook; and RESPA, TILA and TRID. No item asks a student to recall anything from
 * any of them, and every rate and figure in every computational item is supplied inside the item as a given.
 *
 * Course version 1.0 submission draft — NOT APPROVED. No Arizona prelicensure credit is available.
 */

